I now have a complete and thorough picture. One important note: I re-verified the openapi.yml schema and it currently defines a **points-based** model (a `membershipPoints` field plus a `membershipLevel` derived from points, max 4), which does **not** match the actual `MembershipLevelResolver` implementation (additive +1 per factor, capped at 3/4, no points). Here are all the findings.

## 1. Membership-level computation

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/MembershipLevelResolver.java`** — the class that computes the level from the four factors (email present, namesakeCount, household size, tenure days). Key method:

```java
public static int deriveMembershipLevel(String email, Integer namesakeCount,
        Integer householdMemberCount, LocalDate registrationDate) {
    int level = 1;
    if (email != null && !email.isBlank()) {
        level++;
    }
    if (namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0) {
        level++;
    }
    if (householdMemberCount != null && householdMemberCount >= GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE) { // GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE = 3
        level++;
    }
    int maxLevel = hasTenure(registrationDate) ? TENURED_MAX_LEVEL : PRE_TENURE_MAX_LEVEL; // 4 : 3
    return Math.min(level, maxLevel);
}

private static boolean hasTenure(LocalDate registrationDate) {
    if (registrationDate == null) {
        return false;
    }
    return ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS; // 365
}
```

This is an **additive +1-per-factor** model: base 1, +1 email, +1 unique name (namesakeCount==0), +1 household of 3+, capped at 3 unless tenure > 365 days (then cap 4).

## 2. Where the level is wired in / the DTO

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — MapStruct mapper. Line 29-30 maps `membershipLevel` on `OwnerDto` by calling the resolver:
```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipLevel",
    expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.MembershipLevelResolver.deriveMembershipLevel(owner.getEmail(), owner.getNamesakeCount(), owner.getHouseholdMemberCount(), owner.getRegistrationDate()))")
```
Note: it maps `membershipLevel` but **nothing maps `membershipPoints`** (see mismatch below).

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** — the controller. It:
